window.REALMS_DATA = {"version":"0.8","status":"Design-complete draft; not balance-locked; simulation pending","global":{"deck_size":30,"resource_split":{"+1":15,"+2":15},"legendary_per_faction":1,"preserved_core":["5-card recurring selective hand cycle","20 player Health","simultaneous creature-vs-creature combat","alternating combat activations","Realm rules unchanged from v0.7 unless separately revised"],"notes":["Permanent +HP means maximum and current HP unless text explicitly says maximum HP without restoring.","Temporary/static +HP that ends can cause lethal marked damage when maximum HP falls."]},"factions":{"Living Geodes":{"code":"GEO","realm":"Crystal Isle","identity":"Damage creates Pressure. Pressure transforms living crystal from Dormant to Cracked, then pushes the Cracked form toward Folded death.","universal":"PRESSURE - Whenever a Dormant or Cracked Geode takes damage, it gains 1 Pressure for that separate damage event. Pressure from damage resolves before destruction from that damage is checked. When a Dormant Geode reaches its Crack threshold, resolve Pressure triggers, then transform it into its Cracked form and reset its Pressure to 0. Re-evaluate lethal marked damage against the new form. When a Cracked Geode reaches its Fold threshold, resolve any \"gains Pressure\" triggers first, then it becomes Folded and is destroyed.","passives":{"Kimberlite":"KIMBERLITE - Whenever one of your Dormant Geodes Cracks, every other friendly Geode gains 1 Pressure. This may Crack Dormant Geodes or Fold Cracked Geodes and can chain.","Fracture":"FRACTURE - Whenever one of your Cracked Geodes gains Pressure, give 1 Pressure to another random friendly Geode. If that Geode is Cracked, Fracture can trigger again. The chain ends naturally when it reaches a Dormant Geode, no other Geode exists, or Geodes Fold."}},"Harvest":{"code":"HAR","realm":"Deadlands","identity":"Living biomass must keep growing. Growth prevents decay; death or deliberate consumption moves that growth into the survivors.","universal":"LIFEBLOOD - A Harvest creature is Nourished for the round if it gains STR or maximum HP from any friendly effect that round. A Harvest creature that enters play is Nourished for that round. At the end of your round, each friendly Harvest creature that is not Nourished takes 1 Wither damage.","passives":{"Regurgitate":"REGURGITATE - Whenever one of your creatures dies, choose another friendly creature. It permanently gains +1 STR / +1 maximum and current HP.","Consume":"CONSUME - Once per round during Placement, you may destroy one friendly creature. Choose another friendly creature. It permanently gains either STR or maximum and current HP equal to the destroyed creature's printed Cost."}},"Continuum":{"code":"CON","realm":"The Endless","identity":"Time is a persistent 0-5 Sequence. Skip Ahead reaches completion more often; Loop Back spends longer inside the powerful 4/5 window.","universal":"SEQUENCE - Each Continuum player has a visible Sequence counter: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5. It begins at 0. At the start of your round, Shift it 1 step. Combat never changes Sequence unless a card explicitly says so. Reaching 5 triggers every applicable Sequence Complete effect. High Sequence effects are active only while your Sequence is 4 or 5. Static High Sequence stat bonuses disappear immediately when you leave 4/5; if losing a maximum-HP bonus makes marked damage lethal, that creature is destroyed.","passives":{"Skip Ahead":"SKIP AHEAD - Your Sequence normally moves forward 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> 0. Once per round during Placement, discard a card from your hand to the Graveyard to Shift forward 1 additional step.","Loop Back":"LOOP BACK - Your Sequence begins moving forward. When it reaches 5, Sequence Complete triggers and its direction reverses. Future Shifts move 5 -> 4 -> 3 -> 2 -> 1 -> 0. At 0, direction reverses forward again. Thus the natural High Sequence window is 4 -> 5 -> 4. Card effects that say Shift follow the current direction unless they explicitly say otherwise."}},"Moondemons":{"code":"MON","realm":"Blood Moon","identity":"Being wounded turns every card on. Dealing damage feeds the wound, but each Major makes survival dangerous in the opposite direction.","universal":"BLOODIED - A Moondemon below its maximum HP is Bloodied and its printed Bloodied text is active. Whenever a Moondemon deals damage to another target, after that damage resolves restore 2 HP to that Moondemon. Self-damage does not trigger this restore.","passives":{"Bloodthirst":"BLOODTHIRST - At the end of your round, each Bloodied friendly Moondemon loses 1 current HP. If a Moondemon is destroyed by this Bloodthirst loss, every other friendly Moondemon permanently gains +2 STR / +2 maximum and current HP.","Frenzied":"FRENZIED - Whenever a Bloodied friendly Moondemon deals damage to another target, it permanently gains +2 STR / +2 maximum and current HP before its universal 2-HP restore. Once a Moondemon has become Bloodied, if it ever returns to full HP, destroy it immediately."}},"Eliteborn":{"code":"ELI","realm":"Upper Strata","identity":"Creatures and their equipment are connected into explicit Formations. Exact Formation size turns card abilities on and determines how the chosen Major rewards commitment.","universal":"FORMATION - When an Eliteborn Creature enters play, choose whether it begins a new Formation or joins an existing one. Formation size counts Creatures plus attached Equips. Formation (N) means the printed effect is active while that card's Formation is exactly size N; Formation (N+) means N or greater. Equips attach to a Creature, occupy no creature slot, and add 1 to that Creature's Formation size. Each Creature may have only 1 Equip. Equips do not have STR/HP and do not receive creature damage.","passives":{"We Stand Together":"WE STAND TOGETHER - You have 7 creature slots instead of 6. Whenever one of your Formations reaches size 5 or greater, it has Disperse. When a creature in that Format